Z||000000||Doni Hagan||08-06-2001||07:35 PM||||I removed the wing from my GT and the trunk literally FLIES up without the extra weight. I almost got smacked in the mouth when my wife pushed the release button the first time. Is there a way to adjust the spring tension?||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroLisa||08-06-2001||07:47 PM||||Yes there is a way to adjust the tension on the decklid. At the hinge there are pins that adjust the tension. I tightened mine, but if you aren't at the lowest tension, you can change it. Rodney Dickman, with the help of a big long piece of rope, adjusted mine, so I can't tell you too much about how to do it, except that there's a chance to loose a finger or 2  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Steve Normington||08-06-2001||08:30 PM||||Try putting a Slushie on the lid.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||maryjane||08-06-2001||09:03 PM||||Doni, there was a thread about 2 mos ago on this subject, I think started by mach10. I didn't pay too much attention to it (except the slurppy launching), but I think there are different color coded springs to use. Search and ye shall find!<BR>Don||||reg||1
Z||000004||cadaver||08-07-2001||02:16 AM||||Yes there are different springs. I dont know if you can adjust the heavy springs for the wing loose enough to work ok without the weight of the wing.||||reg||1
